  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Coarsely chop the tomatoes. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345300/photos/large/81287_1-71510a51e752e6377ce34db70e9423be.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start stew: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the tomato and garlic, stirring, for 2-3 mins until softened. Add the chickpeas, chipotle, peanut butter, 2 tbs tomato paste and 1 tsp sugar and cook, stirring, for 2 mins or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345301/photos/large/81287_2-024d80c9bdfdb994dbe1b7e9cc11b450.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer stew: Add 125ml (½ cup) water to the chickpea mixture and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook for 5 mins or until slightly thickened. Add the spinach and stir until wilted. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345302/photos/large/81287_3-4659869f427836d02851222d4845bfdb.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soak couscous: Meanwhile, put the couscous in a large heatproof bowl, add a drizzle of olive oil (see Kitchen hack), pour over 200ml boiling water and cover with a plate. Stand for 5 mins or until the water is absorbed. Season generously with salt and pepper, then fluff with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345303/photos/large/81287_4-901489a435619acc7f24d83fae90b3ee.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the couscous and chickpea stew among bowls. Scatter over the peanuts and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345304/photos/large/81287_5-7ccb6a059ddeaaff7d2675437c6a178d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen hack: Adding a little oil to the couscous when soaking adds flavour and helps separate the grains, making the couscous nice and light once you have fluffed it with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1345305/photos/large/81287_6-d63922cc7f95b5f624b8ac4ae5e28715.jpeg"
    }
  ]
